  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "If \n$H=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(H)=$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the rank of $H,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(H)=2.$",
